Perturbational data are especially valuable.

Where possible, separate:

```text
baseline
```

```text
event onset
```

```text
peak response
```

```text
finite-time propagation
```

```text
post-event state
```

```text
recovery
```

```text
residual / hysteresis
```

Ask separately:

* Did state-space location change?
* Did movement change?
* Did local dynamics change?
* Did reachable geometry change?
